  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">350.org Renew our Power Gathering</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ABOUT RENEW OUR POWER
All around the world, people have shown we want a safer planet to pass onto future generations &#x2013; one that runs on renewable, affordable and accessible energy for all.

We know the money for making this happen is there: governments, public funds, development banks, private sector companies and especially those who disproportionately drive the climate crisis &#x2013; the mega polluters and ultra-rich &#x2013; are some key players that need to fund the upgrade of our energy systems towards fair and accessible renewables. And not only that: they should ensure those least served by the current failed system are the first in line to benefit from a just energy transition.

The Renew Our Power Gathering is a hybrid event that will connect thousands of people from around the world through keynote events, workshops, and cultural sessions to catalyze renewable energy projects led by and in favor of communities.

We don&#x2019;t want just new energy systems, but better and more democratic ones: taking power away from fossil fuel corporations, and putting it in the hands of people. And, together, we can achieve it.

It&#x2019;s time to reclaim our power to rebuild our world!
We need to act now, with speed and in scale. Renew Our Power will equip our movement to rapidly boost a just energy transition across the globe!</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">350.org</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">350Africa.org is the lead organization of the Fair Finance Coalition in South Africa. It is part of an international movement working to end the age of fossil fuels and build a world of community-led renewable energy for all.

The organization uses grassroots organizing to run locally-driven campaigns in every corner of the globe. A small team of paid staff supports grassroots activists running their own independent, loosely affiliated organizations and campaigns across the continent.

350Africa.org believes that the onlyway we&#x2019;ll see meaningful action on climate change is if we can counter the power of the fossil fuel industry with the power of people taking collective action.

The head office is based in the USA. The branch in South Africa is legally established in South Africa. The internal systems are fully integrated in the central 350.0rg systems.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
